<h2>Segment 208 &mdash; the mind-only position</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s208S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w1">gnyis pa</span> la <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w2">gnyis</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w3">gzhan</span> gyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w4">lugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w5">brjod pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s208w6">dang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w7">lugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w8">de</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w9">dgag pa</span>&#x27;o, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w10">dang po</span> ni, de <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w11">skad</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w12">bstan pa</span> yin dang slar yang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w13">sems tsam pas</span> rang gi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w14">lugs</span> brjod pa <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w15">gtso bor</span> byas pa <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s208w16">nyid kyis</span> rang gi &#x27;dod don &#x27;grub par <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w17">bsams</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s208w18">shing</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w19">smras pa</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s208S">. . .The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w1">second</span> part has <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w2">two</span> sections of its own: <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w5">stating</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w4">position</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w3">other</span> school, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s208w6">and then</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w9">denying</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w8">this</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w7">position</span>. Here is the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w10">first</span>. This is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w11">how</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w12">presentation</span> was made. Then those of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w13">Mind-Only School</span> come back, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w17">considering</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s208w18">and then</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w19">presenting</span> a position which <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s208w16">by itself</span> reflects the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w15">primary</span> belief of their entire <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s208w14">system</span>.</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Codex Tibetan-first PROVISIONAL machine alignment. The final assertion is a compressed recasting: rang gi lugs brjod pa and rang gi 'dod don 'grub par are distributed across position, reflects, belief and system. Only securely attributable lexical pieces are selected; omitted pieces are not asserted absent. Supplied part, sections, school after other, Here is the, and those of the remain unwrapped. slar yang contributes the return sense of come back but is omitted because its adverb-to-verb recast is less secure. No nulls are manufactured.</div>
